<title>USA: Glaxo submits application for nasal spray.</title>
<headline>Glaxo submits application for nasal spray.</headline>
<dateline>RESEARCH TRIANGLE PARK, N.C. 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Glaxo Wellcome Inc said Thursday it has submitted a supplementary new drug application to the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to market Flonase nasal spray for treating 4- to 11-year-olds.</p>
<p>Flonase is currently indicated as a treatment for nasal allergies for people 12 years old and older, the company said.</p>
<p>The company said Flonase was safe and effective overall when studied in five clinical trials involving 1,152 children aged four to 11.</p>
</text>
